            <ArticleTitle>Acute appendicitis presenting as acute left scrotal pain: diagnostic considerations.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>634-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>To our knowledge this is the first case of acute perforated appendicitis presenting as acute left scrotal pain described in the literature. In addition, this case involved a unique false positive radionuclide scrotal scan for testicular torsion, which is also reported and discussed for the first time.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
